WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.034 --> 00:00:02.968
-My next guest is
an Emmy, Grammy,

00:00:02.968 --> 00:00:04.837
and Tony-winning performer

00:00:04.837 --> 00:00:07.907
who you can see in the third
and final season of "Pose,"

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:10.543
which airs Sundays
at 10:00 p.m. on FX.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.578
Please welcome Billy Porter!

00:00:12.578 --> 00:00:14.180
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.781
♪ -Billy Porter ♪

00:00:15.781 --> 00:00:18.017
♪ Everybody knows ♪

00:00:18.017 --> 00:00:20.085
♪ You're shining like a star ♪

00:00:20.085 --> 00:00:22.288
♪ When you strike a pose ♪

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:24.023
♪ Billy Porter ♪

00:00:24.023 --> 00:00:26.459
♪ Casting a spell ♪

00:00:26.459 --> 00:00:28.261
♪ On the audience ♪

00:00:28.261 --> 00:00:30.796
♪ When you turn into Pray Tell ♪

00:00:30.796 --> 00:00:32.165
♪ Yeah ♪

00:00:32.165 --> 00:00:33.599
-I knew it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:33.599 --> 00:00:35.468
-I'm coming to "Fallon."

00:00:35.468 --> 00:00:37.069
-Billy Porter, come on.

00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.872
-I know you like my clothes.
I'm coming to "Fallon."

00:00:39.872 --> 00:00:41.608
I call it Sissy Pimp.

00:00:41.608 --> 00:00:45.177
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.177 --> 00:00:46.980
My Sissy Pimp look.

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:48.381
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:51.517
-I want to show you an Instagram
photo, because I follow you.

00:00:51.517 --> 00:00:53.686
And you're a great follow.

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.488
This is you cleaning the pool.

00:00:55.488 --> 00:00:56.489
[ Laughter ]

00:00:56.489 --> 00:00:58.691
This is how Billy Porter
cleans his pool.

00:00:58.691 --> 00:01:00.793
[ Laughter ]
-Please!

00:01:00.793 --> 00:01:04.063
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:06.465
Listen. Listen.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.402
That is a photo shoot
in Palm Springs.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.172
It's Emilio Pucci realness.
-Okay.

00:01:12.172 --> 00:01:15.941
-I didn't have a pool
when I shot that.

00:01:15.941 --> 00:01:19.512
I do have a pool now.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:21.347
And somebody else cleans it!

00:01:21.347 --> 00:01:22.648
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Oh, come on!

00:01:22.648 --> 00:01:25.418
That's what I'm talking about!

00:01:25.418 --> 00:01:27.587
-I don't clean the pool, kids!

00:01:27.587 --> 00:01:30.422
I don't clean the pool.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:30.422 --> 00:01:31.957
-I want to talk to you about
a bunch of things.

00:01:31.957 --> 00:01:33.393
But I want to talk to you about

00:01:33.393 --> 00:01:35.794
this "Hollywood Reporter"
article.

00:01:35.794 --> 00:01:38.997
This was amazing, actually.
It was powerful.

00:01:38.997 --> 00:01:42.335
It says, "This is what
HIV-positive looks like now."

00:01:42.335 --> 00:01:43.736
-Yes.

00:01:43.736 --> 00:01:46.573
-We all didn't know, obviously.

00:01:46.573 --> 00:01:49.108
You were HIV-positive
for 14 years?

00:01:49.108 --> 00:01:52.945
-Yeah, I've been positive
since 2007.

00:01:52.945 --> 00:01:59.185
And, you know, having lived
through the AIDS crisis,

00:01:59.185 --> 00:02:00.753
it was heavy for me.

00:02:00.753 --> 00:02:02.721
It was a heavy year, 2007.

00:02:02.721 --> 00:02:08.061
And I lived with the shame of it
for a really long time,

00:02:08.061 --> 00:02:10.596
and last week,
I released that shame.

00:02:10.596 --> 00:02:12.798
I released that trauma.

00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:16.135
And I am a free man, honey!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:16.135 --> 00:02:18.070
Free. Free.
-It feels good?

00:02:18.070 --> 00:02:20.906
-Yes, it does. It does.

00:02:20.906 --> 00:02:27.780
I've never -- I've never -- I've
never felt joy like this before.

00:02:27.780 --> 00:02:31.517
And, you know, we talk about it
in the black church.

00:02:31.517 --> 00:02:33.586
You know, this joy that I have,

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:36.388
the world didn't give it and
the world can't take it away.

00:02:36.388 --> 00:02:38.157
I got it.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:40.092
I got some joy now.
-I'm so happy.

00:02:40.092 --> 00:02:42.561
-You know, and it's just --
it really feels good.

00:02:42.561 --> 00:02:44.097
It really feels great.

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:46.833
-I thought it was
very brave of you.

00:02:46.833 --> 00:02:49.368
But also,
what an interesting story.

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:50.870
And I can't even imagine

00:02:50.870 --> 00:02:53.405
how anyone would
just deal with that and just --

00:02:53.405 --> 00:02:56.241
I mean, your mom -- you didn't
even tell your mother.

00:02:56.241 --> 00:02:58.311
-No.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:58.311 --> 00:02:59.679
That was the thing, you know.

00:02:59.679 --> 00:03:01.480
It's, like, growing up
in the Pentecostal church,

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:03.582
there's such a stigma
surrounding it.

00:03:03.582 --> 00:03:05.985
You know, having lived
through it, you know,

00:03:05.985 --> 00:03:08.387
I was supposed to know better,
it happened anyway.

00:03:08.387 --> 00:03:10.890
You know, there was just so much
going on, and my mother

00:03:10.890 --> 00:03:19.465
received so much, you know,
persecution because I was gay.

00:03:19.465 --> 00:03:22.535
And I just didn't want her to
have to go through that again.

00:03:22.535 --> 00:03:24.770
It's sort of like
a second coming-out.

00:03:24.770 --> 00:03:26.872
And I didn't want her
to go through that again,

00:03:26.872 --> 00:03:28.974
and my sister and I had vowed

00:03:28.974 --> 00:03:31.177
we were just going to wait
till she was dead.

00:03:31.177 --> 00:03:35.915
And she went into a nursing home
six years ago,

00:03:35.915 --> 00:03:37.350
and she ain't going nowhere.

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:39.352
[ Laughter ]
She's full of life!

00:03:39.352 --> 00:03:40.352
-That's right.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:40.352 --> 00:03:42.255
-So it's time to tell her!

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.757
-Time to tell her, yeah.
-Time to tell her.

00:03:44.757 --> 00:03:47.059
-I know you have --
Last time we talked,

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.728
you said you were
working on music?

00:03:48.728 --> 00:03:50.062
-Yes.
-How's the music?

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:51.597
-New music, honey. New music.

00:03:51.597 --> 00:03:53.299
-No, no. I want this.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:53.299 --> 00:03:55.435
-For those of you
who don't know, you know,

00:03:55.435 --> 00:03:59.305
I had a record deal
back in the '90s -- 1997.

00:03:59.305 --> 00:04:01.707
My first R&amp;B album came out
on A&amp;M Records.

00:04:01.707 --> 00:04:03.709
You know, they put
my gay ass out.

00:04:03.709 --> 00:04:06.645
[ Laughter ]
So I did it anyway.

00:04:06.645 --> 00:04:08.781
And now I'm coming back!
Daddy's coming back!

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:10.083
[ Cheers and applause ]
-That's right.

00:04:10.083 --> 00:04:14.220
-Move out the way,
Ariana Grande, Beyoncé,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.989
you know, Lady Gaga,
all the kids.

00:04:16.989 --> 00:04:18.825
Just make some space for Daddy.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:18.825 --> 00:04:20.693
-Alright.
-I'm coming. Make some space.

00:04:20.693 --> 00:04:22.928
-And you're recording right now?
-I'm recording right now.

00:04:22.928 --> 00:04:24.229
I've been recording
for the last two months.

00:04:24.229 --> 00:04:26.466
We got about 10 songs.

00:04:26.466 --> 00:04:30.670
And I am so thrilled because,
you know, for the first time

00:04:30.670 --> 00:04:34.373
in my life, it's exactly
what I want it to be.

00:04:34.373 --> 00:04:39.278
The music is exactly from me,
what I want to say,

00:04:39.278 --> 00:04:41.147
and the message, and the gift

00:04:41.147 --> 00:04:42.382
that I want to
give to the world,

00:04:42.382 --> 00:04:46.051
which is, you know,
hope, you know, love.

00:04:46.051 --> 00:04:47.720
We have to choose it.

00:04:47.720 --> 00:04:49.789
We have to recommit to it
every day.

00:04:49.789 --> 00:04:52.625
We have to choose it,
so that we can fight,

00:04:52.625 --> 00:04:55.894
you know,
the evil that is pervasive.

00:04:55.894 --> 00:04:58.464
You know, we can only fight it
with love.

00:04:58.464 --> 00:05:00.833
We can only do that.
It can only change with love.

00:05:00.833 --> 00:05:02.935
And I'm so excited for my music
for that.

00:05:02.935 --> 00:05:05.338
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:05.338 --> 00:05:07.506
-We also talked about --
You're like,

00:05:07.506 --> 00:05:11.510
"I'm just gonna work, work, work
during this pandemic."

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:13.479
And you said,
"I'm working on a memoir."

00:05:13.479 --> 00:05:16.415
I go, "Oh, my gosh."
And I go, "How is the editing?

00:05:16.415 --> 00:05:17.816
How is it going?
How is writing?"

00:05:17.816 --> 00:05:19.085
You're like, "Great."

00:05:19.085 --> 00:05:21.587
You brought to us tonight,
which I'm so thankful,

00:05:21.587 --> 00:05:23.656
the cover of the memoir.

00:05:23.656 --> 00:05:25.658
-You get a first look
of the cover!

00:05:25.658 --> 00:05:27.526
[ Cheers and applause ]
She's done!

00:05:27.526 --> 00:05:28.961
-Alright, here we go.
-The book is done!

00:05:28.961 --> 00:05:31.997
-Ready?
-Ow!

00:05:31.997 --> 00:05:32.999
Ah!

00:05:32.999 --> 00:05:35.701
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:35.701 --> 00:05:38.104
-Look at that.
-Pre-order!

00:05:38.104 --> 00:05:39.138
-Pre-order!

00:05:39.138 --> 00:05:40.840
-I need the children
to pre-order.

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.908
-Pre-order! Oh, my God.

00:05:42.908 --> 00:05:45.111
-I need to be on
the best-seller list, y'all.

00:05:45.111 --> 00:05:46.245
-It's going to happen.
That's all it takes.

00:05:46.245 --> 00:05:50.382
-Daddy got to pay that mortgage.
-Exactly.

00:05:50.382 --> 00:05:52.584
I want to talk about "Pose,"
too, while you're here.

00:05:52.584 --> 00:05:54.152
You have so many projects.

00:05:54.152 --> 00:05:55.688
This is the final season
of "Pose."

00:05:55.688 --> 00:05:57.790
-Yes.
-But you kind of always planned

00:05:57.790 --> 00:05:59.558
this out to be
the final season, correct?

00:05:59.558 --> 00:06:01.194
-Well, I didn't plan anything.

00:06:01.194 --> 00:06:03.128
[ Laughter ]

00:06:03.128 --> 00:06:09.034
The creators, Steven Canals and
Ryan Murphy and Brad Falchuk,

00:06:09.034 --> 00:06:13.506
you know, they always intended
for the story to end

00:06:13.506 --> 00:06:16.876
when the antiretroviral drugs
came out.

00:06:16.876 --> 00:06:18.077
And that was '96.

00:06:18.077 --> 00:06:21.447
And, you know, there wasn't
really a limit,

00:06:21.447 --> 00:06:23.916
but as we told the story,
you know,

00:06:23.916 --> 00:06:25.718
they realized,
"Oh, we're there."

00:06:25.718 --> 00:06:28.587
And, you know, the show
is too important

00:06:28.587 --> 00:06:30.823
to continue it
just because it's a hit.

00:06:30.823 --> 00:06:33.759
-Yeah.
-It matters too much.

00:06:33.759 --> 00:06:37.930
You know, this season is --
I think it's exceptional.

00:06:37.930 --> 00:06:41.867
You know, I keep saying, you
know, just for me personally,

00:06:41.867 --> 00:06:48.707
you know, I got to use "Pose"
and Pray Tell as a proxy,

00:06:48.707 --> 00:06:50.342
you know, for my healing.

00:06:50.342 --> 00:06:51.510
-Oh, interesting.

00:06:51.510 --> 00:06:54.814
-And, you know,
I've been saying,

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:58.484
if I don't ever
do anything else --

00:06:58.484 --> 00:07:00.886
and I'm already doing
a lot of other things --

00:07:00.886 --> 00:07:06.825
but if I don't ever do anything
in my life -- else in my life,

00:07:06.825 --> 00:07:09.628
I will have done it, you know?

00:07:09.628 --> 00:07:11.296
It's --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:07:11.296 --> 00:07:13.265
I've said everything
I've needed to say,

00:07:13.265 --> 00:07:16.035
and now it's time to tell
a different story.

00:07:16.035 --> 00:07:18.971
Now I get to tell a different
story, and I'm excited about it.

00:07:18.971 --> 00:07:20.806
-I love you, bud.
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:07:20.806 --> 00:07:23.475
Here's Billy Porter in "Pose."
Take a look.

00:07:23.475 --> 00:07:24.977
-I loved you.

00:07:24.977 --> 00:07:27.379
And I'm not ashamed of
what you once meant to me,

00:07:27.379 --> 00:07:29.715
but you're asking me
to step away from the church.

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.184
-No, no, no, no, the church
stepped away from me.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:33.853
And I'm not the only one.

00:07:33.853 --> 00:07:38.390
Every year I watch hundreds
of kids flock to the city,

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:45.364
looking for what they lost after
the church threw them away.

00:07:45.364 --> 00:07:47.132
That's what your church d--

00:07:47.132 --> 00:07:53.372
♪♪

00:07:53.372 --> 00:07:57.210
That's what your church did.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:07:58.844
To me.

00:07:58.844 --> 00:08:01.780
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:01.780 --> 00:08:03.749
-Billy Porter!

00:08:03.749 --> 00:08:06.018
Amazing. Amazing.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:06.018 --> 00:08:11.056
The final season of "Pose" airs
Sundays at 10:00 p.m. on FX.

00:08:11.056 --> 00:08:13.693
Look for the music!
Look for the book!

